# Scripts run on Linux (CI, WSL) as well as on Windows. A carriage return in a shell script breaks a Linux bash
# ("syntax error near unexpected token `{\r'"), and with core.autocrlf=true Git would write CRLF into the working tree.
# These patterns make Git write LF for them on every machine; tests/repo/line-endings.spec.ts checks it.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.sql text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
scripts/** text eol=lf
tools/*/scripts/** text eol=lf
.github/workflows/*.yml text eol=lf
